cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use OpenBijli software or its tariff data, please cite it using the
  metadata below. Attribute the data as "OpenBijli contributors, tariff data
  (CC BY 4.0)".
type: software
title: "OpenBijli: open Indian electricity tariff data, bill engine and rooftop solar simulator"
abstract: >-
  OpenBijli is a versioned, source-linked dataset of Indian household
  electricity tariffs (one JSON tariff book per regulator and financial year,
  with citations to the page of each tariff order), a TypeScript bill engine,
  a rooftop solar right-sizing and payback simulator, an evidence engine for
  billing disputes, and Meter Sakshi, a non-contact check meter that reads an
  electricity meter's pulse LED. Release 0.1.0 covers 9 tariff books and 25
  utilities for FY 2026-27. The code is licensed under MIT; the tariff data in
  data/ under CC BY 4.0; the Meter Sakshi hardware designs under
  CERN-OHL-P-2.0.
authors:
  - name: "OpenBijli contributors"
repository-code: "https://github.com/byjoellobo/openbijli"
url: "https://byjoellobo.github.io/openbijli/"
license: MIT
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-11-03"
keywords:
  - india
  - electricity
  - tariff
  - electricity bill
  - discom
  - rooftop solar
  - net metering
  - PM Surya Ghar
  - smart meter
  - prepaid meter
  - open data
  - energy policy
